{ Now I will show you some of the best traps that come up at the Italian Opening.

Let's start with the Legal Trap (Play Nc3) } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gb1c3] }
1. Nc3 Bg4 { How do we attack that bishop? } 2. h3 { Excellent! } 2... Bh5 { Can you find the incredible sacrifice you have now? } 3. Nxe5 { Very well! Now we lose the queen, but Black loses the game. } 3... Bxd1 { Can you find the mate sequence in 2? } 4. Bxf7+ { That's right! } 4... Ke7 { And now, the final move! } 5. Nd5# { My favorite trap.
I have made a compilation of the best 10 traps in the Italian opening that you can see by clicking here: https://lichess.org/study/Iaef8Vtb } { [%cal Bf7e8,Bf7e6,Bd5e7,Be5f7,Bd5f6,Be5d7] } *

